# Refactor: Split `app/models.py`

This plan addresses section 2.5 of the improvement analysis, which notes that `app/models.py` is too large (1034 lines) and should be split into domain-grouped files.

## Proposed Changes

We will create a new directory `app/models/` and split the monolithic `app/models.py` into logical groups. We will create `app/models/__init__.py` to re-export all models so existing imports throughout the application (e.g., `from app.models import User, Employee`) will not break.

### 1. `app/models/core.py`
Contains foundational models shared across modules.
- `Module`, `UserModule`, `User`, `AuditLog`, `LoginHistory`, `Notification`, `Holiday`
- Also contains `validate_password_complexity`

### 2. `app/models/hr.py`
Contains Admin/HR configuration models.
- `Department`, `Designation`, `Shift`, `LeavePolicy`, `AttendanceRule`

### 3. `app/models/employee.py`
Contains employee records and self-service domain models.
- `Employee`, `Leave`, `LeaveBalance`, `Attendance`, `AttendanceRegularization`, `CompOff`, `ShiftSwapRequest`, `Timesheet`, `ProfileUpdateRequest`, `EmployeeDocument`

### 4. `app/models/pm.py`
Contains Project Management models.
- `Project`, `ProjectMember`, `Task`, `Milestone`

### 5. `app/models/recruitment.py`
Contains recruitment tracking.
- `JobPosting`, `Candidate`, `Interview`

### 6. `app/models/performance.py`
Contains performance evaluation models.
- `PerformanceReview`

### 7. `app/models/finance.py`
Contains finance and payroll models.
- `Expense`, `EmployeeExpense`, `Invoice`, `SalaryRecord`, `PayrollInput`

### 8. `app/models/__init__.py`
Will import and re-export all the above classes, for example:
```python
from .core import User, Module, UserModule, AuditLog, LoginHistory, Notification, Holiday, validate_password_complexity
from .hr import Department, Designation, Shift, LeavePolicy, AttendanceRule
from .employee import Employee, Leave, LeaveBalance, Attendance, AttendanceRegularization, CompOff, ShiftSwapRequest, Timesheet, ProfileUpdateRequest, EmployeeDocument
from .pm import Project, ProjectMember, Task, Milestone
from .recruitment import JobPosting, Candidate, Interview
from .performance import PerformanceReview
from .finance import Expense, EmployeeExpense, Invoice, SalaryRecord, PayrollInput
```

### 9. Delete `app/models.py`
Once the new module is thoroughly verified, the old monolithic file will be deleted.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]  
> This is a major structural change. While we will ensure all `db.relationship` and `db.ForeignKey` bindings use strings to prevent circular imports, separating models can sometimes reveal hidden dependencies. Please review the proposed domain separation to ensure it aligns with your architectural goals.

## Verification Plan

- After splitting, we will use the `run_command` tool to execute `python -c "from app import create_app; app = create_app(); print('App loaded successfully')"` to verify that SQLAlchemy can resolve all relationships without cyclic import errors.
- We will also run `python -c "from app.models import User, Employee; print('Models imported')"` to ensure the `__init__.py` re-export works correctly.
